# No comments on new / changed code

**Default:** do not add `//`, `/* */`, or `/** */` in files you touch. Code must stand without narration.

Also strip **commented-out code** (disabled lines that used to run).

## Gate (before claiming done)

Your **diff** must have no new comments unless they already existed and you did not touch that line.

| Delete | Example |
|---|---|
| Narration | `// 400, not 422 — FE shows generic toast` |
| Docblock on obvious method | `/** No silent 000 fallback … */` |
| Disabled code | `// $oldVar = $this->legacyMethod();` |
| Why-I-chose-this | `// this message needs to reach the user as-is` |

**Keep only (do not add new ones):**
- License headers already in the file
- Existing comments you did not introduce

If a status code or message needs explaining, put it in `ResponseMessage` / a short method name — not a comment.

## Examples

### Bad (never land)

```php
/** No silent 000 fallback — wrong branch = wrong report data. */
private function requireBranchCode(array $data): string
{
    if ($branchCode === '') {
        // 400, not 422 — FE shows a generic toast on 422
        throw new InsException(ResponseMessage::HOME_BRANCH_MISSING, 400);
    }
}
```

```js
// 400 = explicit setup problem — show it as-is
if (status === 400 && data?.message) {
```

### Good

```php
private function requireBranchCode(array $data): string
{
    if ($branchCode === '') {
        throw new InsException(ResponseMessage::HOME_BRANCH_MISSING, 400);
    }
}
```

```js
if (status === 400 && data?.message) {
```

## Hook

`.githooks/check-commented-code.mjs` warns on staged PHP/JS/Vue (does not block). Review before push.

## Coexistence

- Same bar as `04-simple-code-voice.mdc` (no narration comments).
- Does not replace humanizer (`commit-humanizer.mdc`).
